  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved labour migration governance in Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Labour migration from Nigeria continues to expand, offering important opportunities for employment and development, while also presenting challenges related to governance gaps, protection of migrant workers, and risks of exploitation. This CPO addresses the need to strengthen labour migration governance systems to ensure safe, orderly, and regular migration in line with international labour standards.

During the biennium, the expected results are improved labour migration governance frameworks and enhanced capacity of national stakeholders to effectively design, implement, and monitor gender-responsive policies, laws, and mechanisms that protect migrant workers throughout the migration cycle, including recruitment, employment, return, and reintegration. It also promotes fair recruitment practices, strengthens enforcement and oversight systems, and improves access to information, grievance, and justice mechanisms.

The primary beneficiaries include migrant workers and their families, as well as government institutions, employers&#x2019; and workers&#x2019; organizations, civil society actors, and the media involved in labour migration governance. The programme contributes to empowering migrant workers to make informed decisions, reducing vulnerabilities to exploitation, and enhancing access to protection and support services.

The CPO is implemented in collaboration with key international and development partners, as well as through engagement with regional and interregional mechanisms that support labour migration. It emphasizes capacity development, social dialogue, policy coherence, and strengthened coordination between origin and destination countries. Overall, it contributes to transparent, accountable, and rights-based labour migration systems that promote decent work and deliver mutually beneficial outcomes for workers, employers, and societies.</narrative>
  </description>
